window.IELTS_DATA.items.push(...[{"section":"writing-general","title":"Application for an internship","prompt":"You have recently learned about an opening for an internship at a local company that you are interested in.\n\nWrite a letter to the director of the company. In your letter,\n- introduce yourself\n- explain how you learned about the internship\n- explain why you would be suitable for the internship","answer":"Dear Ms Carter,\n\n<strong class=\"key-phrase\">I am writing to apply for</strong> the marketing internship recently advertised on your company&#x27;s careers page. I am currently completing the final year of a business degree at Hanoi University, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">with a particular focus on</strong> digital communication and consumer behaviour.\n\nI <strong class=\"key-phrase\">learned about the position through</strong> a presentation given by one of your former interns at a university careers event. Her description of the company&#x27;s practical training and collaborative culture <strong class=\"key-phrase\">strongly encouraged me to apply</strong>.\n\nI believe I would be <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a suitable candidate</strong> for three reasons. First, I have managed social-media content for a student organisation and increased event registrations through <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a targeted campaign</strong>. Second, my coursework has given me <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a solid foundation</strong> in market research and data analysis. Finally, I am <strong class=\"key-phrase\">comfortable working in English</strong> and have experience presenting ideas to both small groups and large audiences.\n\nI have attached my CV and would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I could contribute to your team. <strong class=\"key-phrase\">Thank you for considering my application</strong>.\n\nYours sincerely,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"I am writing to apply for","context":"I am writing to apply for the marketing internship recently advertised on your company's careers page. I am currently completing the final year of a business degree at Hanoi University, with a particular focus on digital communication and consumer behaviour."},{"en":"with a particular focus on","context":"I am writing to apply for the marketing internship recently advertised on your company's careers page. I am currently completing the final year of a business degree at Hanoi University, with a particular focus on digital communication and consumer behaviour."},{"en":"learned about the position through","context":"I learned about the position through a presentation given by one of your former interns at a university careers event. Her description of the company's practical training and collaborative culture strongly encouraged me to apply."},{"en":"strongly encouraged me to apply","context":"I learned about the position through a presentation given by one of your former interns at a university careers event. Her description of the company's practical training and collaborative culture strongly encouraged me to apply."},{"en":"a suitable candidate","context":"I believe I would be a suitable candidate for three reasons. First, I have managed social-media content for a student organisation and increased event registrations through a targeted campaign. Second, my coursework has given me a solid foundation in market research and data analysis. Finally, I am comfortable working in English and have experience presenting ideas to both small groups and large audiences."},{"en":"a targeted campaign","context":"I believe I would be a suitable candidate for three reasons. First, I have managed social-media content for a student organisation and increased event registrations through a targeted campaign. Second, my coursework has given me a solid foundation in market research and data analysis. Finally, I am comfortable working in English and have experience presenting ideas to both small groups and large audiences."},{"en":"a solid foundation","context":"I believe I would be a suitable candidate for three reasons. First, I have managed social-media content for a student organisation and increased event registrations through a targeted campaign. Second, my coursework has given me a solid foundation in market research and data analysis. Finally, I am comfortable working in English and have experience presenting ideas to both small groups and large audiences."},{"en":"comfortable working in English","context":"I believe I would be a suitable candidate for three reasons. First, I have managed social-media content for a student organisation and increased event registrations through a targeted campaign. Second, my coursework has given me a solid foundation in market research and data analysis. Finally, I am comfortable working in English and have experience presenting ideas to both small groups and large audiences."},{"en":"Thank you for considering my application","context":"I have attached my CV and would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I could contribute to your team. Thank you for considering my application."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Application for an internship","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-001","_displayNo":"#001"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Applying for a part-time restaurant job","prompt":"A local restaurant is recruiting a part-time employee.\n\nWrite to the restaurant manager. In your letter:\n- apply for the position\n- describe relevant experience\n- state the days and hours you can work","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\n<strong class=\"key-phrase\">I am writing to apply for</strong> the part-time front-of-house position advertised in the window of Green Table Restaurant.\n\nI have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">eighteen months of relevant customer-service experience</strong> from working at a busy cafe near my university. My duties included taking orders, handling card payments, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">resolving minor complaints</strong> and preparing the dining area between sittings. The role taught me to remain polite and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">work efficiently under pressure</strong>, even during crowded weekend shifts. I also hold a current food-safety certificate and speak both English and Vietnamese fluently.\n\nI am available from 5 p.m. until closing on Monday, Wednesday and Friday, and at any time on Saturday or Sunday. During university holidays, I could take additional daytime shifts if required.\n\nI would welcome the opportunity to discuss the position and am <strong class=\"key-phrase\">available for interview</strong> this week. My CV and the contact details of my previous supervisor are attached.\n\n<strong class=\"key-phrase\">Thank you for considering my application</strong>.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"I am writing to apply for","context":"I am writing to apply for the part-time front-of-house position advertised in the window of Green Table Restaurant."},{"en":"eighteen months of relevant customer-service experience","context":"I have eighteen months of relevant customer-service experience from working at a busy cafe near my university. My duties included taking orders, handling card payments, resolving minor complaints and preparing the dining area between sittings. The role taught me to remain polite and work efficiently under pressure, even during crowded weekend shifts. I also hold a current food-safety certificate and speak both English and Vietnamese fluently."},{"en":"resolving minor complaints","context":"I have eighteen months of relevant customer-service experience from working at a busy cafe near my university. My duties included taking orders, handling card payments, resolving minor complaints and preparing the dining area between sittings. The role taught me to remain polite and work efficiently under pressure, even during crowded weekend shifts. I also hold a current food-safety certificate and speak both English and Vietnamese fluently."},{"en":"work efficiently under pressure","context":"I have eighteen months of relevant customer-service experience from working at a busy cafe near my university. My duties included taking orders, handling card payments, resolving minor complaints and preparing the dining area between sittings. The role taught me to remain polite and work efficiently under pressure, even during crowded weekend shifts. I also hold a current food-safety certificate and speak both English and Vietnamese fluently."},{"en":"available for interview","context":"I would welcome the opportunity to discuss the position and am available for interview this week. My CV and the contact details of my previous supervisor are attached."},{"en":"Thank you for considering my application","context":"Thank you for considering my application."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Applying for a part-time restaurant job","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-002","_displayNo":"#002"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Complaint about a faulty camera","prompt":"You bought a camera that was faulty, returned it to the shop and were promised a repair, but a week later it is still not ready.\n\nWrite to the company. In your letter:\n- introduce yourself and the purchase\n- explain what has happened\n- state what action you expect","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nMy name is Alex Morgan, and I am writing regarding a Lumix G90 camera purchased from your King Street branch on 2 June, receipt number KS-7714.\n\nThe camera appeared normal in the shop, but at home the shutter repeatedly froze and several photographs were saved with a black band across the image. I returned it the following day, and your representative assured me that the repair would take no more than three working days.\n\nIt has now been eight days, and staff cannot tell me when the camera will be ready. This delay is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">no longer acceptable</strong> because I bought the equipment for a paid photography assignment next weekend. I have already given the shop <strong class=\"key-phrase\">ample opportunity</strong> to resolve the fault.\n\nI would therefore like either a new replacement of the same specification or <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a full refund</strong>. If neither can be arranged by Friday, I will have to hire another camera and may seek reimbursement for that cost. I hope the matter can be brought to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a prompt resolution</strong>.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"no longer acceptable","context":"It has now been eight days, and staff cannot tell me when the camera will be ready. This delay is no longer acceptable because I bought the equipment for a paid photography assignment next weekend. I have already given the shop ample opportunity to resolve the fault."},{"en":"ample opportunity","context":"It has now been eight days, and staff cannot tell me when the camera will be ready. This delay is no longer acceptable because I bought the equipment for a paid photography assignment next weekend. I have already given the shop ample opportunity to resolve the fault."},{"en":"a full refund","context":"I would therefore like either a new replacement of the same specification or a full refund. If neither can be arranged by Friday, I will have to hire another camera and may seek reimbursement for that cost. I hope the matter can be brought to a prompt resolution."},{"en":"a prompt resolution","context":"I would therefore like either a new replacement of the same specification or a full refund. If neither can be arranged by Friday, I will have to hire another camera and may seek reimbursement for that cost. I hope the matter can be brought to a prompt resolution."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Complaint about a faulty camera","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-003","_displayNo":"#003"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Complaint about a theatre visit","prompt":"You attended a good play at a theatre but could not enjoy it because of problems at the venue.\n\nWrite to the theatre manager. In your letter:\n- identify the performance and date\n- describe the problems\n- suggest what should be done","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI am writing about the evening performance of The Last Station at the Grand Theatre on Friday, 5 June.\n\nThe play itself was excellent, but the experience was <strong class=\"key-phrase\">seriously undermined by several problems</strong>. When my partner and I arrived, another couple had been allocated the same seats. An usher moved us to the front row, where a stage light shone directly into our eyes throughout the first act. In addition, the air-conditioning was not working, and the auditorium became uncomfortably hot.\n\nI appreciate that isolated technical problems occur, but <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a double-booking error should have been resolved</strong> before the performance began. The replacement seats were clearly unsuitable, yet staff did not offer us another option or explain how to make a complaint.\n\nI suggest reviewing the booking system, checking lighting positions before each show and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">training ushers to handle seating errors consistently</strong>. Given the disruption, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">I would also consider a partial refund</strong> or replacement tickets to be <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a reasonable remedy</strong>.\n\nI look forward to your response.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"seriously undermined by several problems","context":"The play itself was excellent, but the experience was seriously undermined by several problems. When my partner and I arrived, another couple had been allocated the same seats. An usher moved us to the front row, where a stage light shone directly into our eyes throughout the first act. In addition, the air-conditioning was not working, and the auditorium became uncomfortably hot."},{"en":"a double-booking error should have been resolved","context":"I appreciate that isolated technical problems occur, but a double-booking error should have been resolved before the performance began. The replacement seats were clearly unsuitable, yet staff did not offer us another option or explain how to make a complaint."},{"en":"training ushers to handle seating errors consistently","context":"I suggest reviewing the booking system, checking lighting positions before each show and training ushers to handle seating errors consistently. Given the disruption, I would also consider a partial refund or replacement tickets to be a reasonable remedy."},{"en":"I would also consider a partial refund","context":"I suggest reviewing the booking system, checking lighting positions before each show and training ushers to handle seating errors consistently. Given the disruption, I would also consider a partial refund or replacement tickets to be a reasonable remedy."},{"en":"a reasonable remedy","context":"I suggest reviewing the booking system, checking lighting positions before each show and training ushers to handle seating errors consistently. Given the disruption, I would also consider a partial refund or replacement tickets to be a reasonable remedy."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Complaint about a theatre visit","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-004","_displayNo":"#004"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Complaint about noise at a recreation ground","prompt":"A school regularly brings pupils to a recreation ground near your home, and recent visits have caused problems.\n\nWrite to the head teacher. In your letter:\n- explain why you enjoy living near the ground\n- describe the recent problems\n- suggest what the school should do","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI live opposite Maple Recreation Ground and am writing about the sports sessions held there by pupils from your school.\n\nResidents generally value the open space because it provides trees, walking paths and a safe place for local children to play. We also understand that school sport is valuable and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">have never objected to normal daytime activity</strong>.\n\nHowever, during the past three weeks, several groups have left plastic bottles and food packaging behind. Footballs have repeatedly struck parked cars, and pupils have gathered outside nearby houses shouting for up to thirty minutes after the sessions ended. These incidents <strong class=\"key-phrase\">disrupt local residents</strong>, particularly older people and parents with young children.\n\nCould teachers please <strong class=\"key-phrase\">supervise pupils more closely</strong>, ensure all rubbish is collected and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">keep pupils within the marked playing area</strong>? It would also help if groups left promptly once the lesson had finished. These simple measures would allow the school to continue using the ground <strong class=\"key-phrase\">without creating unnecessary conflict</strong>.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"have never objected to normal daytime activity","context":"Residents generally value the open space because it provides trees, walking paths and a safe place for local children to play. We also understand that school sport is valuable and have never objected to normal daytime activity."},{"en":"disrupt local residents","context":"However, during the past three weeks, several groups have left plastic bottles and food packaging behind. Footballs have repeatedly struck parked cars, and pupils have gathered outside nearby houses shouting for up to thirty minutes after the sessions ended. These incidents disrupt local residents, particularly older people and parents with young children."},{"en":"supervise pupils more closely","context":"Could teachers please supervise pupils more closely, ensure all rubbish is collected and keep pupils within the marked playing area? It would also help if groups left promptly once the lesson had finished. These simple measures would allow the school to continue using the ground without creating unnecessary conflict."},{"en":"keep pupils within the marked playing area","context":"Could teachers please supervise pupils more closely, ensure all rubbish is collected and keep pupils within the marked playing area? It would also help if groups left promptly once the lesson had finished. These simple measures would allow the school to continue using the ground without creating unnecessary conflict."},{"en":"without creating unnecessary conflict","context":"Could teachers please supervise pupils more closely, ensure all rubbish is collected and keep pupils within the marked playing area? It would also help if groups left promptly once the lesson had finished. These simple measures would allow the school to continue using the ground without creating unnecessary conflict."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Complaint about noise at a recreation ground","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-005","_displayNo":"#005"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Complaint about noisy neighbours","prompt":"You live in an apartment building but are having trouble with the behaviour of your neighbours.\n\nWrite a letter to inform the building manager of the situation. In your letter,\n- explain who you are\n- describe the situation concerning your neighbours' behaviour\n- suggest how the situation could be dealt with","answer":"Dear Building Manager,\n\nI am a resident of apartment 8B and am writing to report repeated late-night noise from apartment 8C. The problem has continued for nearly three weeks and is now seriously affecting my sleep and ability to work.\n\nThe occupants frequently <strong class=\"key-phrase\">play loud music</strong> and move furniture between midnight and 2 a.m. Last Saturday, a large gathering continued until almost 3 a.m., despite two polite requests from nearby residents to reduce the noise. I fully understand that people should be able to enjoy their homes, but the current situation is unreasonable in <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a shared building</strong>.\n\n<strong class=\"key-phrase\">I would be grateful if you could</strong> remind the residents of the building&#x27;s quiet-hours policy and speak to them directly. If the disturbance continues, a written warning may be necessary. It may also be useful to circulate the policy to all residents so that expectations are <strong class=\"key-phrase\">clear and consistent</strong>.\n\nPlease let me know what action will be taken. I am available to provide a dated record of the incidents if required.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"play loud music","context":"The occupants frequently play loud music and move furniture between midnight and 2 a.m. Last Saturday, a large gathering continued until almost 3 a.m., despite two polite requests from nearby residents to reduce the noise. I fully understand that people should be able to enjoy their homes, but the current situation is unreasonable in a shared building."},{"en":"a shared building","context":"The occupants frequently play loud music and move furniture between midnight and 2 a.m. Last Saturday, a large gathering continued until almost 3 a.m., despite two polite requests from nearby residents to reduce the noise. I fully understand that people should be able to enjoy their homes, but the current situation is unreasonable in a shared building."},{"en":"I would be grateful if you could","context":"I would be grateful if you could remind the residents of the building's quiet-hours policy and speak to them directly. If the disturbance continues, a written warning may be necessary. It may also be useful to circulate the policy to all residents so that expectations are clear and consistent."},{"en":"clear and consistent","context":"I would be grateful if you could remind the residents of the building's quiet-hours policy and speak to them directly. If the disturbance continues, a written warning may be necessary. It may also be useful to circulate the policy to all residents so that expectations are clear and consistent."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Complaint about noisy neighbours","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-006","_displayNo":"#006"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Complaint about sports-centre changing rooms","prompt":"The changing rooms at a sports centre are in poor condition. You have complained before but nothing has changed.\n\nWrite to the manager. In your letter:\n- describe the problems\n- explain what happened after earlier complaints\n- state what action you expect","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI am writing to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make a formal complaint</strong> about the changing rooms at Greenfield Sports Centre.\n\nSeveral lockers no longer close properly, two showers have been leaking for weeks, and the floor is frequently covered in water. The broken ventilation system has also created a strong smell and visible mould near the ceiling. These conditions are unpleasant and, more importantly, pose a safety risk.\n\nI have <strong class=\"key-phrase\">raised this issue repeatedly</strong> at reception during the past month. Each time, I was told that maintenance had been informed, yet no repairs have been completed and no warning signs have been placed near the wet floor.\n\nI would like the centre to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">take immediate corrective action</strong> by repairing the showers and lockers, cleaning the affected areas thoroughly and publishing a clear timetable for the ventilation work. Until the floor is safe, staff should inspect it regularly and place appropriate signs where necessary.\n\nPlease respond within seven days with details of the action you intend to take.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"make a formal complaint","context":"I am writing to make a formal complaint about the changing rooms at Greenfield Sports Centre."},{"en":"raised this issue repeatedly","context":"I have raised this issue repeatedly at reception during the past month. Each time, I was told that maintenance had been informed, yet no repairs have been completed and no warning signs have been placed near the wet floor."},{"en":"take immediate corrective action","context":"I would like the centre to take immediate corrective action by repairing the showers and lockers, cleaning the affected areas thoroughly and publishing a clear timetable for the ventilation work. Until the floor is safe, staff should inspect it regularly and place appropriate signs where necessary."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Complaint about sports-centre changing rooms","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-007","_displayNo":"#007"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Disputing an increase in car insurance","prompt":"Your insurer has informed you that your monthly car-insurance payment will increase, and you disagree with the decision.\n\nWrite to the insurer. In your letter:\n- explain why you are writing\n- state why the increase seems unjustified\n- say what you want the company to do","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI am writing regarding your notice dated 10 June, which states that my monthly car-insurance premium will rise by 28 per cent from August.\n\nI would ask you to review this decision because my circumstances do not appear to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">justify such a substantial increase</strong>. I have held policy number MC-44821 for six years and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">maintained a completely claim-free record</strong>. My vehicle, annual mileage and home address have not changed, and the car is parked overnight in a locked garage. I have also completed an approved defensive-driving course since my last renewal.\n\nPlease provide a <strong class=\"key-phrase\">clear breakdown</strong> of the factors used to calculate the new premium. If the increase resulted from incorrect information, I would like the policy amended immediately. If it reflects a general pricing change, please reconsider the quotation <strong class=\"key-phrase\">in light of</strong> my history and confirm whether <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a higher excess or revised level of cover</strong> would reduce the cost.\n\nI look forward to receiving a written response before the current policy expires.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"justify such a substantial increase","context":"I would ask you to review this decision because my circumstances do not appear to justify such a substantial increase. I have held policy number MC-44821 for six years and maintained a completely claim-free record. My vehicle, annual mileage and home address have not changed, and the car is parked overnight in a locked garage. I have also completed an approved defensive-driving course since my last renewal."},{"en":"maintained a completely claim-free record","context":"I would ask you to review this decision because my circumstances do not appear to justify such a substantial increase. I have held policy number MC-44821 for six years and maintained a completely claim-free record. My vehicle, annual mileage and home address have not changed, and the car is parked overnight in a locked garage. I have also completed an approved defensive-driving course since my last renewal."},{"en":"clear breakdown","context":"Please provide a clear breakdown of the factors used to calculate the new premium. If the increase resulted from incorrect information, I would like the policy amended immediately. If it reflects a general pricing change, please reconsider the quotation in light of my history and confirm whether a higher excess or revised level of cover would reduce the cost."},{"en":"in light of","context":"Please provide a clear breakdown of the factors used to calculate the new premium. If the increase resulted from incorrect information, I would like the policy amended immediately. If it reflects a general pricing change, please reconsider the quotation in light of my history and confirm whether a higher excess or revised level of cover would reduce the cost."},{"en":"a higher excess or revised level of cover","context":"Please provide a clear breakdown of the factors used to calculate the new premium. If the increase resulted from incorrect information, I would like the policy amended immediately. If it reflects a general pricing change, please reconsider the quotation in light of my history and confirm whether a higher excess or revised level of cover would reduce the cost."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Disputing an increase in car insurance","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-008","_displayNo":"#008"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Documents left in a taxi","prompt":"You accidentally left important papers in a taxi.\n\nWrite to the taxi company. In your letter:\n- give details of the journey\n- explain why the papers matter\n- request specific help from the company","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI am writing to report a blue document case that I left in one of your taxis yesterday evening.\n\nI was collected outside City Hospital at approximately 6.20 p.m. and travelled to 18 King Street. I paid by card at 6.45 p.m., and the receipt shows journey reference TX-80417. I was seated in the rear left-hand seat and believe the case slipped onto the floor when I got out.\n\nIt contains signed employment forms, certified copies of my qualifications and other time-sensitive documents required for a visa appointment on Thursday. Some of these documents would take several weeks to replace.\n\nCould you please use the payment reference to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">trace the vehicle</strong> and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">contact the driver directly</strong>? I would be happy to collect the case from your office or meet the driver at a convenient location. A member of your staff can reach me on 07700 123456 at any time today.\n\nThank you for treating this matter as urgent.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"trace the vehicle","context":"Could you please use the payment reference to trace the vehicle and contact the driver directly? I would be happy to collect the case from your office or meet the driver at a convenient location. A member of your staff can reach me on 07700 123456 at any time today."},{"en":"contact the driver directly","context":"Could you please use the payment reference to trace the vehicle and contact the driver directly? I would be happy to collect the case from your office or meet the driver at a convenient location. A member of your staff can reach me on 07700 123456 at any time today."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Documents left in a taxi","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-009","_displayNo":"#009"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Enquiring about a conference centre","prompt":"Your employer is planning a training course and has asked you to check whether a local conference centre is suitable.\n\nWrite to the centre manager. In your letter:\n- describe the course\n- list the equipment and facilities required\n- ask further questions about the venue","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\n<strong class=\"key-phrase\">I am writing to enquire about</strong> hiring the Lakeside Conference Centre for a two-day staff training course in October.\n\nThe programme will focus on customer-service skills and is expected to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">accommodate approximately</strong> forty-five participants. We would require one main room <strong class=\"key-phrase\">arranged in cabaret style</strong> and two smaller rooms for group exercises. The course would run from 9 a.m. to 4.30 p.m. on both days.\n\nPlease confirm whether the venue provides reliable Wi-Fi, a projector, wireless microphones and other audio-visual equipment. We would also need flip charts, movable tables and access to printing facilities. Tea, coffee and a light lunch should be available for all participants, including several people with dietary restrictions.\n\nCould you let me know whether parking is included, whether the building is fully accessible and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">what cancellation terms apply</strong>? I would also appreciate an <strong class=\"key-phrase\">itemised quotation</strong> covering room hire, equipment and catering.\n\nIf the centre is available on 15–16 October, I would be pleased to arrange a site visit next week.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"I am writing to enquire about","context":"I am writing to enquire about hiring the Lakeside Conference Centre for a two-day staff training course in October."},{"en":"accommodate approximately","context":"The programme will focus on customer-service skills and is expected to accommodate approximately forty-five participants. We would require one main room arranged in cabaret style and two smaller rooms for group exercises. The course would run from 9 a.m. to 4.30 p.m. on both days."},{"en":"arranged in cabaret style","context":"The programme will focus on customer-service skills and is expected to accommodate approximately forty-five participants. We would require one main room arranged in cabaret style and two smaller rooms for group exercises. The course would run from 9 a.m. to 4.30 p.m. on both days."},{"en":"what cancellation terms apply","context":"Could you let me know whether parking is included, whether the building is fully accessible and what cancellation terms apply? I would also appreciate an itemised quotation covering room hire, equipment and catering."},{"en":"itemised quotation","context":"Could you let me know whether parking is included, whether the building is fully accessible and what cancellation terms apply? I would also appreciate an itemised quotation covering room hire, equipment and catering."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Enquiring about a conference centre","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-010","_displayNo":"#010"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Important papers left at a hotel","prompt":"After attending a meeting at a hotel, you realised that you had left important documents behind.\n\nWrite to the hotel manager. In your letter:\n- state where you may have left the documents\n- explain why they are important\n- say what you would like the manager to do","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI attended a business meeting at the Riverside Hotel yesterday and believe I left a folder containing important documents in the building.\n\nThe meeting took place in the Oak Conference Room from 2 p.m. to 5 p.m. I was seated near the window and may have left the folder either under my chair or on the table beside the projector. It is dark grey and marked “Northgate Project”.\n\nThe folder contains signed contracts and confidential documents relating to a client tender that closes on Friday. <strong class=\"key-phrase\">Replacing the originals would be difficult</strong> and could delay the submission, so <strong class=\"key-phrase\">I would be grateful if</strong> a member of staff could check the meeting room as soon as possible. Please also ask the reception desk and housekeeping team whether it has been handed in.\n\nIf the folder is found, could you <strong class=\"key-phrase\">keep it securely at reception</strong>? I can collect it this afternoon. Alternatively, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">I will cover the cost</strong> if you need to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">send it by registered post</strong> to my office.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"Replacing the originals would be difficult","context":"The folder contains signed contracts and confidential documents relating to a client tender that closes on Friday. Replacing the originals would be difficult and could delay the submission, so I would be grateful if a member of staff could check the meeting room as soon as possible. Please also ask the reception desk and housekeeping team whether it has been handed in."},{"en":"I would be grateful if","context":"The folder contains signed contracts and confidential documents relating to a client tender that closes on Friday. Replacing the originals would be difficult and could delay the submission, so I would be grateful if a member of staff could check the meeting room as soon as possible. Please also ask the reception desk and housekeeping team whether it has been handed in."},{"en":"keep it securely at reception","context":"If the folder is found, could you keep it securely at reception? I can collect it this afternoon. Alternatively, I will cover the cost if you need to send it by registered post to my office."},{"en":"I will cover the cost","context":"If the folder is found, could you keep it securely at reception? I can collect it this afternoon. Alternatively, I will cover the cost if you need to send it by registered post to my office."},{"en":"send it by registered post","context":"If the folder is found, could you keep it securely at reception? I can collect it this afternoon. Alternatively, I will cover the cost if you need to send it by registered post to my office."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Important papers left at a hotel","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-011","_displayNo":"#011"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Improving parking at an office building","prompt":"Your office building has no adequate parking for employees.\n\nWrite to the building manager. In your letter:\n- explain the current problem\n- suggest a solution\n- describe how better parking would help staff","answer":"Dear Mr Lewis,\n\nI am writing on behalf of several employees regarding the lack of parking at Westgate Business Centre.\n\nAt present, only twelve spaces are available for more than eighty staff members. The surrounding streets have strict time limits, and the nearest public car park is almost twenty minutes away on foot. This has become <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a daily source of frustration</strong>, particularly for employees who begin early shifts or need to transport equipment.\n\nOne practical solution would be to lease part of the <strong class=\"key-phrase\">unused land</strong> behind the building and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">introduce a permit system</strong> for staff. If this is not immediately possible, the centre could negotiate discounted monthly passes with the Riverside car park and reserve a few existing spaces for employees with mobility needs.\n\nImproved parking would save staff time at the start of the day, make the building more accessible and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">improve punctuality</strong>. It would also prevent staff from moving their cars during working hours to avoid penalties.\n\nI would <strong class=\"key-phrase\">welcome the opportunity to discuss</strong> these options with you and provide a list of employees who would use the scheme.\n\nYours sincerely,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"a daily source of frustration","context":"At present, only twelve spaces are available for more than eighty staff members. The surrounding streets have strict time limits, and the nearest public car park is almost twenty minutes away on foot. This has become a daily source of frustration, particularly for employees who begin early shifts or need to transport equipment."},{"en":"unused land","context":"One practical solution would be to lease part of the unused land behind the building and introduce a permit system for staff. If this is not immediately possible, the centre could negotiate discounted monthly passes with the Riverside car park and reserve a few existing spaces for employees with mobility needs."},{"en":"introduce a permit system","context":"One practical solution would be to lease part of the unused land behind the building and introduce a permit system for staff. If this is not immediately possible, the centre could negotiate discounted monthly passes with the Riverside car park and reserve a few existing spaces for employees with mobility needs."},{"en":"improve punctuality","context":"Improved parking would save staff time at the start of the day, make the building more accessible and improve punctuality. It would also prevent staff from moving their cars during working hours to avoid penalties."},{"en":"welcome the opportunity to discuss","context":"I would welcome the opportunity to discuss these options with you and provide a list of employees who would use the scheme."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Improving parking at an office building","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-012","_displayNo":"#012"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Lost watch on a train","prompt":"You left a valuable item on a train.\n\nWrite to the railway company. In your letter:\n- describe the item\n- state where and when you lost it\n- explain what you would like the company to do","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI am writing to report a watch that I believe I left on one of your trains on Monday, 8 June.\n\nThe item is a silver Seiko wristwatch with a dark-blue face and a narrow metal strap. There is a small scratch beside the number six, and the initials “A.M.” are engraved on the back. Although the watch is not especially expensive, it is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">of considerable sentimental value</strong> because it was a graduation gift from my grandfather.\n\nI travelled on the 18:10 service from Manchester Piccadilly to Leeds and was seated in Coach C, seat 24A. I removed the watch while working on my laptop and probably left it on the fold-down table when I got off at Leeds at approximately 19:05.\n\nCould you please check the lost-property records for that service and ask the cleaning team whether the watch was found? If it has been handed in, I can collect it from Leeds station or pay any reasonable postage costs to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">arrange for its return</strong>.\n\nI have attached a photograph of the watch and a copy of my ticket.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"of considerable sentimental value","context":"The item is a silver Seiko wristwatch with a dark-blue face and a narrow metal strap. There is a small scratch beside the number six, and the initials “A.M.” are engraved on the back. Although the watch is not especially expensive, it is of considerable sentimental value because it was a graduation gift from my grandfather."},{"en":"arrange for its return","context":"Could you please check the lost-property records for that service and ask the cleaning team whether the watch was found? If it has been handed in, I can collect it from Leeds station or pay any reasonable postage costs to arrange for its return."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Lost watch on a train","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-013","_displayNo":"#013"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Offering a talk for an international day","prompt":"A local college is holding an international day, and you would like to give a presentation about your country.\n\nWrite to the college principal. In your letter:\n- describe what you would talk about\n- explain why the students would find it useful\n- ask about the arrangements for speakers","answer":"Dear Principal Harris,\n\nI am writing to offer a short presentation about Vietnam for the college&#x27;s international day in September.\n\nMy talk would cover three areas: regional food traditions, the importance of family celebrations, and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">the rapid changes taking place in major cities</strong> such as Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City. I would use photographs, a short video and a few everyday objects to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">bring the subject to life</strong> rather than presenting a list of facts.\n\nI believe the session would be useful because it would <strong class=\"key-phrase\">give students a balanced picture</strong> of a country that is often discussed mainly as a tourist destination. It could also encourage students from different backgrounds to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">compare customs and ask questions about cultural similarities</strong>.\n\nCould you please tell me how long each presentation should be and how many students are expected? I would also like to know the technical requirements, particularly whether a projector, speakers and internet access will be available.\n\nI would be pleased to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">send a brief outline in advance</strong>.\n\nYours sincerely,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"the rapid changes taking place in major cities","context":"My talk would cover three areas: regional food traditions, the importance of family celebrations, and the rapid changes taking place in major cities such as Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City. I would use photographs, a short video and a few everyday objects to bring the subject to life rather than presenting a list of facts."},{"en":"bring the subject to life","context":"My talk would cover three areas: regional food traditions, the importance of family celebrations, and the rapid changes taking place in major cities such as Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City. I would use photographs, a short video and a few everyday objects to bring the subject to life rather than presenting a list of facts."},{"en":"give students a balanced picture","context":"I believe the session would be useful because it would give students a balanced picture of a country that is often discussed mainly as a tourist destination. It could also encourage students from different backgrounds to compare customs and ask questions about cultural similarities."},{"en":"compare customs and ask questions about cultural similarities","context":"I believe the session would be useful because it would give students a balanced picture of a country that is often discussed mainly as a tourist destination. It could also encourage students from different backgrounds to compare customs and ask questions about cultural similarities."},{"en":"send a brief outline in advance","context":"I would be pleased to send a brief outline in advance."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Offering a talk for an international day","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-014","_displayNo":"#014"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Problems with shared college accommodation","prompt":"You share a college room with another student, but the arrangement is making it difficult for you to study.\n\nWrite to the college accommodation officer. In your letter:\n- describe the current situation\n- explain why it is affecting your work\n- state what type of accommodation you would prefer","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\n<strong class=\"key-phrase\">I am writing to request</strong> a change to my current accommodation in West Hall, where I share Room 214 with another student.\n\nAlthough my roommate is friendly, our routines are completely incompatible. He regularly invites several friends into the room late in the evening and often plays online games without headphones. In addition, he works night shifts and returns at around 2 a.m., which wakes me almost every day.\n\nThis situation is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">seriously affecting my ability to study</strong> because I am preparing for final examinations and need several uninterrupted hours of study each evening. I have tried discussing the matter with him, but the improvements have only been temporary. As a result, I am sleeping poorly and have already missed two morning lectures.\n\nI would therefore be grateful if I could move to a single room, ideally in a quieter part of the residence. If no single room is available, I would be willing to share with a student who follows a more regular daytime schedule. I hope the college can help me find <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a quieter environment</strong> <strong class=\"key-phrase\">at your earliest convenience</strong>.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"I am writing to request","context":"I am writing to request a change to my current accommodation in West Hall, where I share Room 214 with another student."},{"en":"seriously affecting my ability to study","context":"This situation is seriously affecting my ability to study because I am preparing for final examinations and need several uninterrupted hours of study each evening. I have tried discussing the matter with him, but the improvements have only been temporary. As a result, I am sleeping poorly and have already missed two morning lectures."},{"en":"a quieter environment","context":"I would therefore be grateful if I could move to a single room, ideally in a quieter part of the residence. If no single room is available, I would be willing to share with a student who follows a more regular daytime schedule. I hope the college can help me find a quieter environment at your earliest convenience."},{"en":"at your earliest convenience","context":"I would therefore be grateful if I could move to a single room, ideally in a quieter part of the residence. If no single room is available, I would be willing to share with a student who follows a more regular daytime schedule. I hope the college can help me find a quieter environment at your earliest convenience."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Problems with shared college accommodation","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-015","_displayNo":"#015"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Requesting help from a language tutor","prompt":"Your children are learning a foreign language at school but require extra support. A friend has recommended a private tutor.\n\nWrite to the tutor. In your letter:\n- explain why you are contacting them\n- describe the areas your children need help with\n- ask about their experience and teaching suggestions","answer":"Dear Ms Patel,\n\nI am writing on the recommendation of my colleague, Sarah Nguyen, to ask whether you could provide additional French tuition for my two children, aged eleven and thirteen.\n\nBoth children understand basic classroom vocabulary, but <strong class=\"key-phrase\">they are falling behind in speaking and listening</strong>. My younger son is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">hesitant to answer questions aloud</strong>, while my daughter finds it difficult to follow normal-speed recordings and often confuses verb endings. Their school teacher believes that regular one-to-one practice would give them the targeted support they need.\n\nCould you please <strong class=\"key-phrase\">outline your experience</strong> of teaching learners in this age group and explain how you normally assess a new student? I would also appreciate your view on whether they should study together or have separate lessons. Ideally, we are looking for one or two sessions each week after 5 p.m.\n\nPlease let me know your fees, availability and any materials the children would need. I would be happy to arrange an introductory meeting <strong class=\"key-phrase\">at your convenience</strong>.\n\nYours sincerely,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"they are falling behind in speaking and listening","context":"Both children understand basic classroom vocabulary, but they are falling behind in speaking and listening. My younger son is hesitant to answer questions aloud, while my daughter finds it difficult to follow normal-speed recordings and often confuses verb endings. Their school teacher believes that regular one-to-one practice would give them the targeted support they need."},{"en":"hesitant to answer questions aloud","context":"Both children understand basic classroom vocabulary, but they are falling behind in speaking and listening. My younger son is hesitant to answer questions aloud, while my daughter finds it difficult to follow normal-speed recordings and often confuses verb endings. Their school teacher believes that regular one-to-one practice would give them the targeted support they need."},{"en":"outline your experience","context":"Could you please outline your experience of teaching learners in this age group and explain how you normally assess a new student? I would also appreciate your view on whether they should study together or have separate lessons. Ideally, we are looking for one or two sessions each week after 5 p.m."},{"en":"at your convenience","context":"Please let me know your fees, availability and any materials the children would need. I would be happy to arrange an introductory meeting at your convenience."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Requesting help from a language tutor","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-016","_displayNo":"#016"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Suggestions for improving a public library","prompt":"Your local public library has asked users to suggest improvements to its services and facilities.\n\nWrite to the librarian. In your letter:\n- describe what you value about the library\n- explain what could be improved\n- suggest practical changes","answer":"Dear Sir or Madam,\n\nI am writing in response to your request for suggestions about the future development of Central Library.\n\nThe library is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a valuable community resource</strong>. I particularly value the knowledgeable staff, the quiet study area on the first floor and the wide selection of newspapers and reference books. The online reservation system is also straightforward and saves users a great deal of time.\n\nHowever, some facilities currently fall short of users’ needs. There are too few power sockets for laptop users, several chairs are worn and uncomfortable, and the building closes at 6 p.m. on weekdays, which is inconvenient for people who work full time. The children&#x27;s section also becomes extremely crowded at weekends.\n\nI would recommend installing additional charging points and replacing the oldest furniture. It would also be helpful to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">extend the opening hours</strong> until at least 8 p.m. on two or three weekdays. Finally, a small booking system for children&#x27;s activities could prevent overcrowding and allow staff to plan sessions more effectively.\n\nThank you for inviting public feedback. I hope these suggestions are useful.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"a valuable community resource","context":"The library is a valuable community resource. I particularly value the knowledgeable staff, the quiet study area on the first floor and the wide selection of newspapers and reference books. The online reservation system is also straightforward and saves users a great deal of time."},{"en":"extend the opening hours","context":"I would recommend installing additional charging points and replacing the oldest furniture. It would also be helpful to extend the opening hours until at least 8 p.m. on two or three weekdays. Finally, a small booking system for children's activities could prevent overcrowding and allow staff to plan sessions more effectively."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Suggestions for improving a public library","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-017","_displayNo":"#017"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Trying to reconnect with a childhood friend","prompt":"You saw a newspaper article about a childhood friend whom you have not contacted for many years.\n\nWrite to the editor. In your letter:\n- identify the article and edition\n- explain how you lost contact\n- ask for help reconnecting with your friend","answer":"Dear Editor,\n\nI am writing about the profile of Dr Linh Tran published in the Sunday edition of the City Herald on 14 June.\n\nLinh and I were close friends at Nguyen Du Secondary School, but we lost touch after her family moved overseas in 2008. At the time, neither of us used social media regularly, and the email address I had for her later stopped working. I have tried searching professional networks, but I have not been able to confirm whether the person I found is the same Linh.\n\nThe details in your article, particularly the name of her school and her interest in environmental science, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">strongly suggest that she is my former classmate</strong>. I understand that <strong class=\"key-phrase\">you cannot disclose private contact information</strong>. However, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">I would be grateful if you could</strong> <strong class=\"key-phrase\">forward my details</strong> to her on my behalf. She could then decide whether she wishes to respond.\n\nYour assistance could <strong class=\"key-phrase\">put us back in contact</strong> after nearly two decades, and I would greatly appreciate it.\n\nYours faithfully,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Formal","phrases":[{"en":"strongly suggest that she is my former classmate","context":"The details in your article, particularly the name of her school and her interest in environmental science, strongly suggest that she is my former classmate. I understand that you cannot disclose private contact information. However, I would be grateful if you could forward my details to her on my behalf. She could then decide whether she wishes to respond."},{"en":"you cannot disclose private contact information","context":"The details in your article, particularly the name of her school and her interest in environmental science, strongly suggest that she is my former classmate. I understand that you cannot disclose private contact information. However, I would be grateful if you could forward my details to her on my behalf. She could then decide whether she wishes to respond."},{"en":"I would be grateful if you could","context":"The details in your article, particularly the name of her school and her interest in environmental science, strongly suggest that she is my former classmate. I understand that you cannot disclose private contact information. However, I would be grateful if you could forward my details to her on my behalf. She could then decide whether she wishes to respond."},{"en":"forward my details","context":"The details in your article, particularly the name of her school and her interest in environmental science, strongly suggest that she is my former classmate. I understand that you cannot disclose private contact information. However, I would be grateful if you could forward my details to her on my behalf. She could then decide whether she wishes to respond."},{"en":"put us back in contact","context":"Your assistance could put us back in contact after nearly two decades, and I would greatly appreciate it."}],"subtype":"Formal","summary":"Trying to reconnect with a childhood friend","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-018","_displayNo":"#018"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Advice about choosing work instead of college","prompt":"A friend has asked whether they should attend college or start working. You think employment would suit them better.\n\nWrite to your friend. In your letter:\n- explain why college may not suit them\n- describe the advantages of getting a job\n- suggest suitable kinds of work","answer":"Hi Jenny,\n\nIt was great to hear from you. I&#x27;ve thought carefully about your choice, and I honestly think starting work would suit you better than going <strong class=\"key-phrase\">straight to college</strong>.\n\nYou have always been <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a practical, hands-on learner</strong>, whereas most college courses involve long lectures, extensive reading and several years of theoretical study. I&#x27;m not saying you couldn&#x27;t succeed, but I suspect you&#x27;d <strong class=\"key-phrase\">find that environment frustrating</strong> and lose motivation quite quickly.\n\nA job would allow you to gain real-world experience, earn your own money and discover which type of work you genuinely enjoy. It would also give you more independence, and you could still take a professional course later once you have a clearer goal.\n\nBecause you&#x27;re confident, organised and good with people, I&#x27;d look at customer service, hotel reception or event support. An apprenticeship in sales or digital marketing might also be worth considering because it <strong class=\"key-phrase\">combines training with paid work</strong>.\n\nOf course, the final choice is yours, but there&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">no one-size-fits-all answer</strong>. Starting work now doesn&#x27;t close the door to education in the future.\n\nTake care,\nAlex","topic":"Informal","phrases":[{"en":"straight to college","context":"It was great to hear from you. I've thought carefully about your choice, and I honestly think starting work would suit you better than going straight to college."},{"en":"a practical, hands-on learner","context":"You have always been a practical, hands-on learner, whereas most college courses involve long lectures, extensive reading and several years of theoretical study. I'm not saying you couldn't succeed, but I suspect you'd find that environment frustrating and lose motivation quite quickly."},{"en":"find that environment frustrating","context":"You have always been a practical, hands-on learner, whereas most college courses involve long lectures, extensive reading and several years of theoretical study. I'm not saying you couldn't succeed, but I suspect you'd find that environment frustrating and lose motivation quite quickly."},{"en":"combines training with paid work","context":"Because you're confident, organised and good with people, I'd look at customer service, hotel reception or event support. An apprenticeship in sales or digital marketing might also be worth considering because it combines training with paid work."},{"en":"no one-size-fits-all answer","context":"Of course, the final choice is yours, but there's no one-size-fits-all answer. Starting work now doesn't close the door to education in the future."}],"subtype":"Informal","summary":"Advice about choosing work instead of college","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-019","_displayNo":"#019"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Changing plans for a cinema trip","prompt":"You arranged to see a film with a friend, but you can no longer go. Another friend can take your place.\n\nWrite to your friend. In your letter:\n- explain why you cannot attend\n- say who can go instead\n- explain why they would be good company","answer":"Hi Ben,\n\nI&#x27;m really sorry, but <strong class=\"key-phrase\">something urgent has come up</strong> and I won&#x27;t be able to see the film with you on Saturday evening. My manager has asked me to cover a client presentation at short notice, and the meeting cannot be moved because the client is flying home on Sunday.\n\nThe good news is that Minh can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">step in at short notice</strong>. I checked with him before writing, and he&#x27;s free at 7 p.m. He&#x27;s already seen the first film in the series, so you won&#x27;t have to explain the story, and he has offered to collect the tickets from the machine before you arrive.\n\nI think you two will <strong class=\"key-phrase\">get on really well</strong>. You both love science-fiction films, follow the same football team and have a very similar sense of humour. I&#x27;ve given Minh your number, and he&#x27;ll message you tomorrow to confirm where to meet.\n\nI&#x27;m disappointed to miss it, but let&#x27;s arrange another evening next week. Dinner is on me to make up for changing the plan.\n\nAll the best,\nAlex","topic":"Informal","phrases":[{"en":"something urgent has come up","context":"I'm really sorry, but something urgent has come up and I won't be able to see the film with you on Saturday evening. My manager has asked me to cover a client presentation at short notice, and the meeting cannot be moved because the client is flying home on Sunday."},{"en":"step in at short notice","context":"The good news is that Minh can step in at short notice. I checked with him before writing, and he's free at 7 p.m. He's already seen the first film in the series, so you won't have to explain the story, and he has offered to collect the tickets from the machine before you arrive."},{"en":"get on really well","context":"I think you two will get on really well. You both love science-fiction films, follow the same football team and have a very similar sense of humour. I've given Minh your number, and he'll message you tomorrow to confirm where to meet."}],"subtype":"Informal","summary":"Changing plans for a cinema trip","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-020","_displayNo":"#020"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Dog care while on holiday","prompt":"You are going on holiday next week and you need to ask your friend to watch your dog while you are away.\n\nWrite a letter to your friend. In your letter,\n- state how long you will be away\n- tell them what needs to be done\n- state how you will compensate them","answer":"Hi Daniel,\n\nI hope you&#x27;re well. I&#x27;m writing to ask whether you could look after my dog, Milo, while I&#x27;m away in Da Nang from 12 to 19 July. You know him well, so I think staying with you would be far less stressful for him than going to a kennel.\n\nHis routine is simple. He needs a thirty-minute walk every morning and evening, fresh water throughout the day, and one cup of dry food at 7 a.m. and another at 6 p.m. I&#x27;ve left his food, lead and vet&#x27;s number in a labelled box by the front door. Please also give him his allergy tablet every second evening.\n\nI know this is <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a significant favour</strong>, and I don&#x27;t want you to be <strong class=\"key-phrase\">out of pocket</strong>. I&#x27;ll cover all expenses and take you out for dinner when I return. I&#x27;d also be happy to help with your house move next month.\n\nThanks for considering it. Please let me know whether this arrangement would work for you.\n\nBest,\nAlex","topic":"Informal","phrases":[{"en":"a significant favour","context":"I know this is a significant favour, and I don't want you to be out of pocket. I'll cover all expenses and take you out for dinner when I return. I'd also be happy to help with your house move next month."},{"en":"out of pocket","context":"I know this is a significant favour, and I don't want you to be out of pocket. I'll cover all expenses and take you out for dinner when I return. I'd also be happy to help with your house move next month."}],"subtype":"Informal","summary":"Dog care while on holiday","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-021","_displayNo":"#021"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Friend visiting from overseas","prompt":"Your friend from overseas is coming to visit you next month.\n\nWrite a letter to your friend. In your letter,\n- tell them what they need to bring\n- tell them what they will be doing during the time they are visiting\n- warn them about some things that might be challenging","answer":"Hi Maya,\n\nIt&#x27;s great news that you&#x27;ll be visiting Hanoi next month. The weather will probably be hot and humid, so bring light clothes, comfortable walking shoes and a compact rain jacket. You should also install a local transport app before you arrive because it makes <strong class=\"key-phrase\">getting around much easier</strong>.\n\nI&#x27;ve planned <strong class=\"key-phrase\">a balanced programme</strong> for your stay. We can spend the first day exploring the Old Quarter, visit the Museum of Ethnology on Saturday, and take a day trip to Ninh Binh if the weather is clear. I&#x27;ve also booked a small street-food tour, which should give you a good introduction to Vietnamese cuisine.\n\nThere are two things to be prepared for. Traffic can seem chaotic at first, and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">crossing busy roads requires patience</strong>. In addition, some smaller shops accept cash only, so <strong class=\"key-phrase\">it&#x27;s sensible to carry a modest amount</strong> of Vietnamese currency.\n\nI&#x27;m really looking forward to seeing you and showing you around. Send me your flight details when they are confirmed.\n\nTake care,\nAlex","topic":"Informal","phrases":[{"en":"getting around much easier","context":"It's great news that you'll be visiting Hanoi next month. The weather will probably be hot and humid, so bring light clothes, comfortable walking shoes and a compact rain jacket. You should also install a local transport app before you arrive because it makes getting around much easier."},{"en":"a balanced programme","context":"I've planned a balanced programme for your stay. We can spend the first day exploring the Old Quarter, visit the Museum of Ethnology on Saturday, and take a day trip to Ninh Binh if the weather is clear. I've also booked a small street-food tour, which should give you a good introduction to Vietnamese cuisine."},{"en":"crossing busy roads requires patience","context":"There are two things to be prepared for. Traffic can seem chaotic at first, and crossing busy roads requires patience. In addition, some smaller shops accept cash only, so it's sensible to carry a modest amount of Vietnamese currency."},{"en":"it's sensible to carry a modest amount","context":"There are two things to be prepared for. Traffic can seem chaotic at first, and crossing busy roads requires patience. In addition, some smaller shops accept cash only, so it's sensible to carry a modest amount of Vietnamese currency."}],"subtype":"Informal","summary":"Friend visiting from overseas","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-022","_displayNo":"#022"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"House and pet care during a holiday","prompt":"A friend has agreed to look after your home and pet while you are away.\n\nWrite to your friend. In your letter:\n- give contact details for your trip\n- explain how to care for your pet\n- describe any other household tasks","answer":"Hi Daniel,\n\nThanks again for agreeing to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">keep an eye on</strong> the flat and Milo while I&#x27;m in Da Nang from 12 to 19 July. I will be staying at the Seaview Hotel, and you can reach me on my usual mobile number. If I&#x27;m unavailable, please contact my sister Lan on 0903 555 812.\n\nMilo needs two small meals a day, at about 7 a.m. and 6 p.m. His food is in the lower kitchen cupboard. Please take him for a short walk each evening and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">stick to his usual routine</strong>, as sudden changes tend to upset him. He&#x27;s not allowed on the balcony unless someone is with him.\n\nCould you also water the plants in the living room twice during the week and collect any post from the box downstairs? The rubbish is collected on Tuesday evening, so it&#x27;d be great if you could leave the bin outside then.\n\nPlease <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make yourself at home</strong>; there&#x27;s plenty of food in the fridge, and you&#x27;re welcome to use the television and coffee machine.\n\nAll the best,\nAlex","topic":"Informal","phrases":[{"en":"keep an eye on","context":"Thanks again for agreeing to keep an eye on the flat and Milo while I'm in Da Nang from 12 to 19 July. I will be staying at the Seaview Hotel, and you can reach me on my usual mobile number. If I'm unavailable, please contact my sister Lan on 0903 555 812."},{"en":"stick to his usual routine","context":"Milo needs two small meals a day, at about 7 a.m. and 6 p.m. His food is in the lower kitchen cupboard. Please take him for a short walk each evening and stick to his usual routine, as sudden changes tend to upset him. He's not allowed on the balcony unless someone is with him."},{"en":"make yourself at home","context":"Please make yourself at home; there's plenty of food in the fridge, and you're welcome to use the television and coffee machine."}],"subtype":"Informal","summary":"House and pet care during a holiday","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-023","_displayNo":"#023"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Instructions for looking after a flat","prompt":"A friend will stay in your apartment and look after it while you are away.\n\nWrite to your friend. In your letter:\n- give useful information about the apartment\n- provide important instructions\n- explain what to do if a problem occurs","answer":"Hi Sophie,\n\nThanks for staying in my flat while I&#x27;m away. I thought I&#x27;d <strong class=\"key-phrase\">run through the essentials</strong> before I leave on Friday.\n\nThe spare key is in the lockbox beside the front door; the code is 4821. The hot-water switch is inside the kitchen cupboard, and the Wi-Fi password is written underneath the router. Please use anything in the kitchen and feel free to invite Mark over for dinner.\n\nThe main things are to water the balcony plants every three days, collect the post and keep the place secure whenever you go out. The windows in the bedroom can look closed even when they&#x27;re not locked, so please check them carefully. The rubbish bins are taken downstairs on Wednesday evening.\n\n<strong class=\"key-phrase\">In the unlikely event</strong> of a leak or electrical fault, turn off the main switch beside the fridge and call the building caretaker, Mr Hoang, on 0908 222 410. For anything less urgent, just message me.\n\nHave a comfortable stay, and thanks again for helping.\n\nBest,\nAlex","topic":"Informal","phrases":[{"en":"run through the essentials","context":"Thanks for staying in my flat while I'm away. I thought I'd run through the essentials before I leave on Friday."},{"en":"In the unlikely event","context":"In the unlikely event of a leak or electrical fault, turn off the main switch beside the fridge and call the building caretaker, Mr Hoang, on 0908 222 410. For anything less urgent, just message me."}],"subtype":"Informal","summary":"Instructions for looking after a flat","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-024","_displayNo":"#024"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Selling a television to a friend","prompt":"You want to sell your television and think a friend may be interested.\n\nWrite to your friend. In your letter:\n- explain why you are selling it\n- describe the television\n- suggest when your friend could see it","answer":"Hi Chris,\n\nI remember you mentioned that you were looking for a television for your new flat, so I thought I&#x27;d offer you mine <strong class=\"key-phrase\">before advertising it online</strong>.\n\nI&#x27;m only selling it because I&#x27;m moving into a furnished apartment next month and there&#x27;s already a television there. The one I have is a 43-inch Samsung smart TV, about two years old, and it&#x27;s <strong class=\"key-phrase\">in excellent working order</strong>. The screen has no scratches, the remote is included, and it supports Netflix, YouTube and wireless screen sharing. I still have the original box and receipt.\n\nI paid £420 for it, but I think £230 would be a fair price, especially as you wouldn&#x27;t need to arrange delivery. <strong class=\"key-phrase\">There&#x27;s no pressure at all</strong> if it&#x27;s not what you want.\n\nYou could <strong class=\"key-phrase\">come round and have a look</strong> on Saturday afternoon or Sunday morning. I can connect it to the internet so that you can <strong class=\"key-phrase\">test the picture, sound and apps properly</strong>.\n\nLet me know what suits you.\n\nAll the best,\nAlex","topic":"Informal","phrases":[{"en":"before advertising it online","context":"I remember you mentioned that you were looking for a television for your new flat, so I thought I'd offer you mine before advertising it online."},{"en":"in excellent working order","context":"I'm only selling it because I'm moving into a furnished apartment next month and there's already a television there. The one I have is a 43-inch Samsung smart TV, about two years old, and it's in excellent working order. The screen has no scratches, the remote is included, and it supports Netflix, YouTube and wireless screen sharing. I still have the original box and receipt."},{"en":"There's no pressure at all","context":"I paid £420 for it, but I think £230 would be a fair price, especially as you wouldn't need to arrange delivery. There's no pressure at all if it's not what you want."},{"en":"come round and have a look","context":"You could come round and have a look on Saturday afternoon or Sunday morning. I can connect it to the internet so that you can test the picture, sound and apps properly."},{"en":"test the picture, sound and apps properly","context":"You could come round and have a look on Saturday afternoon or Sunday morning. I can connect it to the internet so that you can test the picture, sound and apps properly."}],"subtype":"Informal","summary":"Selling a television to a friend","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-025","_displayNo":"#025"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Planning the annual staff party","prompt":"Your workplace holds an annual party, and you have been asked to help organise the next one.\n\nWrite to your colleagues. In your letter:\n- explain what should be changed from last year\n- mention what did not work well last time\n- suggest a meeting place and time to plan the event","answer":"Hello everyone,\n\nI am writing so that we can start planning this year&#x27;s staff party before venues become fully booked.\n\nI think we should learn from last year&#x27;s experience and make the event less formal. Last year&#x27;s long speeches delayed dinner, while the fixed seating plan made it difficult for colleagues from different departments to mix. The music was also far too loud during the first hour, so conversation was almost impossible.\n\nThis time, I suggest a shorter welcome, a buffet rather than a set meal, and two simple team activities. We should also appoint one person to coordinate the venue and another to look after the schedule on the night, which would help us <strong class=\"key-phrase\">keep the programme running smoothly</strong>.\n\nCould we <strong class=\"key-phrase\">set aside half an hour</strong> next Wednesday at 4.30 p.m. in Meeting Room 3? I will bring a shortlist of venues and an initial budget. Please send me any dietary requirements or activity ideas before then so that we can discuss them efficiently.\n\nBest regards,\nAlex","topic":"Semi-formal","phrases":[{"en":"keep the programme running smoothly","context":"This time, I suggest a shorter welcome, a buffet rather than a set meal, and two simple team activities. We should also appoint one person to coordinate the venue and another to look after the schedule on the night, which would help us keep the programme running smoothly."},{"en":"set aside half an hour","context":"Could we set aside half an hour next Wednesday at 4.30 p.m. in Meeting Room 3? I will bring a shortlist of venues and an initial budget. Please send me any dietary requirements or activity ideas before then so that we can discuss them efficiently."}],"subtype":"Semi-formal","summary":"Planning the annual staff party","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-026","_displayNo":"#026"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Request to pay rent late","prompt":"You are having financial difficulties and need to ask your landlord for permission to pay this month's rent late.\n\nWrite to your landlord. In your letter:\n- explain the reason\n- state when you will pay\n- explain how you will avoid the problem in future","answer":"Dear Mr Lewis,\n\nI am writing to ask whether I may pay this month&#x27;s rent on 15 July rather than on the usual first day of the month.\n\nThe delay is due to a temporary cash-flow problem. My employer changed its payroll provider last week, and several salaries, including mine, will not be processed until 12 July. I have sufficient income to cover the rent, but the funds will not reach my account before the normal payment date.\n\nI will <strong class=\"key-phrase\">make the full payment</strong> of £950 immediately after my salary is deposited and will send you the transfer confirmation that day. I apologise for the inconvenience and appreciate that regular payment is important.\n\nTo prevent a similar delay, I will keep one month&#x27;s rent in a separate savings account and <strong class=\"key-phrase\">set up a standing order</strong> for future payments. This means the rent will be transferred automatically even if my salary date changes again.\n\nI hope this temporary arrangement is acceptable. Please let me know if you need written confirmation from my employer.\n\nYours sincerely,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Semi-formal","phrases":[{"en":"make the full payment","context":"I will make the full payment of £950 immediately after my salary is deposited and will send you the transfer confirmation that day. I apologise for the inconvenience and appreciate that regular payment is important."},{"en":"set up a standing order","context":"To prevent a similar delay, I will keep one month's rent in a separate savings account and set up a standing order for future payments. This means the rent will be transferred automatically even if my salary date changes again."}],"subtype":"Semi-formal","summary":"Request to pay rent late","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-027","_displayNo":"#027"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Requesting extended leave from work","prompt":"You need more than one month of leave from work for personal reasons.\n\nWrite to your manager. In your letter:\n- explain why and how long you need leave\n- describe how you will remain informed\n- suggest how your work can be covered","answer":"Dear Ms Reynolds,\n\n<strong class=\"key-phrase\">I am writing to request</strong> six weeks of unpaid leave from 3 August to 13 September so that I can support my father during his recovery from major surgery.\n\nHe lives alone in another city and will need help with transport, meals and medical appointments for the first month after leaving hospital. My siblings can assist later, but they are unable to cover the initial period.\n\nI am committed to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">ensuring a smooth handover</strong> during my absence. Before leaving, I will complete the July performance report, <strong class=\"key-phrase\">prepare detailed handover notes</strong> and brief Minh on the two client accounts I currently manage. He has already agreed to <strong class=\"key-phrase\">act as the main contact</strong>, while Hoa can approve routine expenses.\n\nTo keep up to date, I will check email each weekday and join the Monday team meeting remotely whenever possible. I will also be available by phone for genuinely urgent questions, although I will <strong class=\"key-phrase\">avoid interfering with day-to-day decisions</strong>.\n\nI hope this plan provides adequate cover for the department. I would be grateful for an opportunity to discuss the request this week.\n\nYours sincerely,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Semi-formal","phrases":[{"en":"I am writing to request","context":"I am writing to request six weeks of unpaid leave from 3 August to 13 September so that I can support my father during his recovery from major surgery."},{"en":"ensuring a smooth handover","context":"I am committed to ensuring a smooth handover during my absence. Before leaving, I will complete the July performance report, prepare detailed handover notes and brief Minh on the two client accounts I currently manage. He has already agreed to act as the main contact, while Hoa can approve routine expenses."},{"en":"prepare detailed handover notes","context":"I am committed to ensuring a smooth handover during my absence. Before leaving, I will complete the July performance report, prepare detailed handover notes and brief Minh on the two client accounts I currently manage. He has already agreed to act as the main contact, while Hoa can approve routine expenses."},{"en":"act as the main contact","context":"I am committed to ensuring a smooth handover during my absence. Before leaving, I will complete the July performance report, prepare detailed handover notes and brief Minh on the two client accounts I currently manage. He has already agreed to act as the main contact, while Hoa can approve routine expenses."},{"en":"avoid interfering with day-to-day decisions","context":"To keep up to date, I will check email each weekday and join the Monday team meeting remotely whenever possible. I will also be available by phone for genuinely urgent questions, although I will avoid interfering with day-to-day decisions."}],"subtype":"Semi-formal","summary":"Requesting extended leave from work","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-028","_displayNo":"#028"},{"section":"writing-general","title":"Volunteering on a school trip","prompt":"Your child's school is arranging a three-day trip abroad and has asked parents to volunteer.\n\nWrite to the head teacher. In your letter:\n- explain why you would like to join the trip\n- describe how you could help\n- ask for further practical details","answer":"Dear Mrs Brown,\n\nI am writing to volunteer for the three-day school trip to Singapore next month.\n\nI would be <strong class=\"key-phrase\">happy to assist</strong> because my daughter is travelling abroad without family for the first time, and I also believe parent volunteers can make the trip safer and less demanding for staff. I have previously accompanied two local day trips and am comfortable supervising groups of teenagers.\n\nDuring the visit, I could <strong class=\"key-phrase\">take responsibility for</strong> a small group during airport transfers, museum visits and meal breaks. I am trained in first aid and speak conversational Mandarin, which may also be useful if the group needs assistance in public places. In addition, I can help keep attendance records and communicate updates to parents.\n\nBefore confirming, could you please <strong class=\"key-phrase\">clarify the practical arrangements</strong>? I would like to know the travel dates, estimated cost, sleeping arrangements and whether volunteers need a background check or additional insurance.\n\nThank you for considering my offer. I am available to discuss the trip after school any day this week.\n\nYours sincerely,\nAlex Morgan","topic":"Semi-formal","phrases":[{"en":"happy to assist","context":"I would be happy to assist because my daughter is travelling abroad without family for the first time, and I also believe parent volunteers can make the trip safer and less demanding for staff. I have previously accompanied two local day trips and am comfortable supervising groups of teenagers."},{"en":"take responsibility for","context":"During the visit, I could take responsibility for a small group during airport transfers, museum visits and meal breaks. I am trained in first aid and speak conversational Mandarin, which may also be useful if the group needs assistance in public places. In addition, I can help keep attendance records and communicate updates to parents."},{"en":"clarify the practical arrangements","context":"Before confirming, could you please clarify the practical arrangements? I would like to know the travel dates, estimated cost, sleeping arrangements and whether volunteers need a background check or additional insurance."}],"subtype":"Semi-formal","summary":"Volunteering on a school trip","visual":null,"id":"writing-general-029","_displayNo":"#029"}]);
